From bfbba6d2d11ee173bcbe610400c08212c95a7d79 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "E. G. Patrick Bos" <egpbos@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 15:56:25 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] PIPE-3305: add a fingerprint of the geodetic values
 measures() reads

The four tables measures() opens for an observatory or AZELGEO measure are
IERSeop97, IERSpredict, TAI_UTC and Observatories. A sha256 over the numeric
values of the columns that move a zenith distance, limited to the MJD window
56000-61000, identifies the data a recorded reference value came from. The
digest covers table.f0 values only, because table.dat holds VS_CREATE and
VS_DATE stamps. Reference value: 60ece9bd21e01000.
---
 pipeline/infrastructure/utils/casa_data.py    | 62 +++++++++++++++++++
 .../infrastructure/utils/casa_data_test.py    | 14 +++++
 2 files changed, 76 insertions(+)

diff --git a/pipeline/infrastructure/utils/casa_data.py b/pipeline/infrastructure/utils/casa_data.py
